  // ------------------------------------------------------------------ 6 tartarus
  C.push({id:'tartarus',title:'6. Tartarus and the Full Moons',intro:[
    'Tartarus has <b>264 floors in 6 blocks</b> (Thebel, Arqa, Yabbashah, Tziah, Harabah, Adamah; the numbers in the checklist below come from one source and may be a floor or a few days off <span class="vf">verify</span>). Blockades split it and open at set points in the year; boss floors stand throughout and each has a teleporter you can use from the entrance once you have activated it. Grind each night until most enemies on the floor are tired ("distressed") before a Full Moon boss; it is the clearest sign that you are ready. Use "Split up" to let the team collect treasure once the floor is quiet, and scan every enemy you meet. The entrance teleporter also restores HP and SP. The Full Moon list and tips below come mostly from a Persona 3 Portable walkthrough (dates are the same as FES, but I could not check each fight in FES); another source also lists an April 9 Magician fight that I could not confirm <span class="vf">verify</span>. Use your consumables before the end: they stop being useful after the final boss.'],
    items:[
      {id:'tt-blk1',t:'Thebel (floors 2 to 16)',d:'Opens about April 20.',vf:'dates from one source'},
      {id:'tt-blk2',t:'Arqa (floors 17 to 63, two sections)',d:'Opens about May 10 and June 13.',vf:'dates from one source'},
      {id:'tt-blk3',t:'Yabbashah (floors 65 to 113, two sections)',d:'Opens about July 9 and August 8.',vf:'dates from one source'},
      {id:'tt-blk4',t:'Tziah (floors 115 to 163, two sections)',d:'Opens about September 10 and October 6.',vf:'dates from one source'},
      {id:'tt-blk5',t:'Harabah (floors 165 to 213)',d:'Opens about November 6.',vf:'dates from one source'},
      {id:'tt-blk6',t:'Adamah (the final block, about 45 floors)',d:'Opens in early January.',vf:'floor count and date'},
      {id:'tt-top',t:'Climb to the top of Tartarus',d:'All 264 floors in all 6 blocks.'},
      {id:'tt-fm',t:'Beat every Full Moon boss',d:'The Full Moon fights are listed below, one box each.'},
      {id:'fm-01',t:'May 9 · Priestess',d:'Monorail. No weakness; reflects ice and blocks light and dark. Her Tiara helpers heal her, so kill them first.',vf:''},
      {id:'fm-02',t:'Jun 8 · Empress and Emperor',d:'Tartarus entrance. Hit the Emperor with elemental attacks and the Empress with physical ones; both can fall in two turns.',vf:''},
      {id:'fm-03',t:'Jul 7 · Hierophant',d:'Hotel Champs de Fleurs area. Fear is the problem: keep Yukari ready to cure it and stack damage buffs.',vf:'where exactly'},
      {id:'fm-04',t:'Jul 7 · Lovers',d:'The sealed room after the Hierophant. Heartbreaker follows Sexy Dance, so remove Charm quickly.',vf:'where exactly'},
      {id:'fm-05',t:'Aug 6 · Chariot and Justice',d:'Underground bunker. No weakness and blocks light and dark. Justice can instant-kill with light, so block light; bring a cure for Fear and Panic.',vf:''},
      {id:'fm-06',t:'Sep 5 · Hermit',d:'Club Escapade. Bring a Persona that blocks electricity and avoid ones that reflect it.',vf:''},
      {id:'fm-07',t:'Oct 4 · Fortune and Strength',d:'Iwatodai Station. Fortune cannot be targeted until Strength falls; ailments on Fortune can give you an all-out attack.',vf:''},
      {id:'fm-08',t:'Nov 3 · Jin and Takaya',d:'Moonlight Bridge. Take Jin down first: his Mudo kills anyone who does not block dark.',vf:'date'},
      {id:'fm-09',t:'Nov 3 · Hanged Man',d:'Moonlight Bridge. Clear the three statues in one turn with area attacks to reach him.',vf:'date'},
      {id:'fm-10',t:'Jan 31 · Jin (Tartarus, about floor 258)',d:'Reflect his magic with Makarakarn; use debuffs and buffs to speed up.',vf:'floor'},
      {id:'fm-11',t:'Jan 31 · Takaya (Tartarus, about floor 262)',d:'Makarakarn is essential against his elemental spells and Mahamaon/Mamudoon.',vf:'floor'},
      {id:'fm-12',t:'Jan 31 · Nyx Avatar (the top of Tartarus)',d:'About 12 forms with their own strengths, then the true form. Bring two strong Personas with different strengths. When it charges Moonless Gown, do not attack: it is reflected.',vf:'forms and floor'},
      {id:'tt-death',t:'Defeat Death, the reaper that roams the floors',d:'He appears if you linger on a floor (you hear chains). Request 53 asks for it, and it opens the Monad Depths.'},
      {id:'tt-monad',t:'Open and climb the Monad Depths',d:'In FES it opens once you beat the Reaper (request 53); in the original game it opened at the last block.',vf:''},
      {id:'tt-boss',t:'Beat Elizabeth\'s superboss',d:'Elizabeth waits on floor 10 of the Monad Depths; see request 55.',vf:'requirements'},
      {id:'tt-final',t:'Beat the final boss',d:'Ends The Journey.'}]});

